# Architecture Decision Records

This directory contains Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) for the HomeOfThings project.

## What is an ADR?

An ADR is a document that captures an important architectural decision made along with its context and consequences.

## ADR Format

```markdown
# ADR-XXX: Title

## Status
[Proposed | Accepted | Deprecated | Superseded]

## Context
What is the issue we're addressing?

## Decision
What is the change we're proposing?

## Consequences
What are the trade-offs?
```

## Creating a New ADR

1. Copy the template below
2. Name file as `ADR-NNN-short-title.md` (e.g., `ADR-001-use-nx-monorepo.md`)
3. Fill in all sections
4. Set status to "Proposed"
5. After discussion, update status to "Accepted"

## Template

```markdown
# ADR-NNN: [Title]

## Status
Proposed

## Context
[Describe the situation and problem]

## Decision
[Describe the decision made]

## Consequences
[Describe the results and trade-offs]
```

